Staged change for hf.co/spaces/Emtenan/LIMA_RAFT :: hybrid_retrieval.py
NOT APPLIED TO THE LIVE SPACE. Apply together with the index swap.

WHY
The indexes on this branch are built with BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5. The Space
embeds queries with all-MiniLM-L6-v2. Both are 384-dimensional, so Chroma
accepts the query without error and returns confidently-ranked nonsense:
MiniLM query vectors compared against bge passage vectors. There is no
exception, no dimension mismatch, and no log line. Swapping the indexes
without this change is the silent-failure case.

RESOLUTION ORDER
Mirrors pipeline/embed_index.py and pipeline/tokenizer_utils.py: prefer the
local weights directory, fall back to the hub id. The Space must therefore
ship models/bge-small-en-v1.5/ alongside the indexes (or set LIMA_EMBED_MODEL),
otherwise the fallback silently re-downloads a DIFFERENT model and
reintroduces exactly the bug this fixes -- see the assertion note below.

--- a/hybrid_retrieval.py
+++ b/hybrid_retrieval.py
@@
-EMBED_MODEL = 'all-MiniLM-L6-v2'
+# Must match the model the indexes were BUILT with. bge-small-en-v1.5 and
+# all-MiniLM-L6-v2 are both 384-dim, so a mismatch does not raise -- it
+# silently degrades retrieval. Resolution mirrors pipeline/embed_index.py:
+# local weights first, hub id only as a fallback.
+_EMBED_MODEL_NAME = 'bge-small-en-v1.5'
+_LOCAL_EMBED_PATH = BASE_DIR / 'models' / _EMBED_MODEL_NAME
+EMBED_MODEL = os.environ.get(
+    'LIMA_EMBED_MODEL',
+    str(_LOCAL_EMBED_PATH) if _LOCAL_EMBED_PATH.exists() else f'BAAI/{_EMBED_MODEL_NAME}',
+)
+
+# bge models expect an instruction prefix on the QUERY side only; passages
+# are embedded bare, which is how the indexes on this branch were built.
+BGE_QUERY_PREFIX = 'Represent this sentence for searching relevant passages: '

(requires `import os` at module top -- the file does not currently import it)

--- a/hybrid_retrieval.py
+++ b/hybrid_retrieval.py
@@ class HybridRetriever._dense_search
-    def _dense_search(self, query: str, n: int = 20) -> list[str]:
-        embedding = self._embedder.encode(query).tolist()
+    def _dense_search(self, query: str, n: int = 20) -> list[str]:
+        # Query-side prefix, matching how the index was built.
+        embedding = self._embedder.encode(BGE_QUERY_PREFIX + query).tolist()

--- a/hybrid_retrieval.py
+++ b/hybrid_retrieval.py
@@ class HybridRetriever.load
     embedder = SentenceTransformer(EMBED_MODEL, device='cpu')
+    # Fail loudly on the one error this whole change exists to prevent.
+    # 512 is bge-small-en-v1.5; all-MiniLM-L6-v2 is 256. Both are 384-dim,
+    # so dimension alone cannot distinguish them.
+    if embedder.get_sentence_embedding_dimension() != 384:
+        raise RuntimeError(
+            f'embedder dim {embedder.get_sentence_embedding_dimension()} != 384; '
+            f'indexes are 384-dim'
+        )
+    if embedder.max_seq_length != 512:
+        raise RuntimeError(
+            f'embedder max_seq_length={embedder.max_seq_length}, expected 512 for '
+            f'{_EMBED_MODEL_NAME}. A 256 value means all-MiniLM-L6-v2 loaded '
+            f'instead -- same dimension, different vector space, silently wrong '
+            f'retrieval against bge-built indexes.'
+        )
     reranker = CrossEncoder(RERANK_MODEL, device='cpu')

NOTE ON THE ASSERTION
max_seq_length is the discriminator that dimension cannot provide. It turns
the silent failure into a startup crash, which is the correct trade: a Space
that refuses to boot is recoverable, a Space serving plausible wrong doctrine
is not.
